main/glib: disable introspection and sysprof when cross-compiling.

Two independent cross blockers for a self-built (no Chimera binary repo)
arch, found on the Astro armv7 port with glib as a rauc dependency:

1. gobject-introspection is marked !cross in its own template ("cross
   compiling tons of janky hackery"), so -Dintrospection=enabled can
   never be satisfied in a cross build — meson fails with "Dependency
   gobject-introspection-1.0 not found".
2. With -Dsysprof=enabled, the generated glib-2.0.pc carries
   "Requires.private: sysprof-capture-4"; in the cross sysroot no
   package provides that .pc, so every downstream pkg-config lookup of
   glib-2.0/gio-2.0 fails ("Run-time dependency gio-2.0 found: NO")
   even with glib-devel installed.

The later -D wins in meson, so the base args stay untouched. Cross-built
glib ships no .gir/.typelib data and no sysprof hooks; glib-devel's
explicit take list has no introspection-only paths, so packaging is
unaffected. Native builds unchanged.

diff --git a/main/glib/template.py b/main/glib/template.py
index c22e0d0e..25004017 100644
--- a/main/glib/template.py
+++ b/main/glib/template.py
@@ -50,6 +50,17 @@ if self.profile().arch == "riscv64":
     # ftbfs
     configure_args += ["-Dtests=false"]
 
+if self.profile().cross:
+    # gobject-introspection is marked !cross ("tons of janky hackery"),
+    # so a cross glib cannot have introspection data; nothing in a
+    # cross-built (self-hosted arch) repo consumes it either.
+    # sysprof is disabled with it: with it enabled, the generated
+    # glib-2.0.pc carries "Requires.private: sysprof-capture-4", which no
+    # package in a self-built repo provides (sysprof-capture's .pc ships
+    # inside glib-devel on native builds) — every downstream pkg-config
+    # lookup of glib-2.0 then fails.
+    configure_args += ["-Dintrospection=disabled", "-Dsysprof=disabled"]
+
 
 def post_install(self):
     from cbuild.util import python
